{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.AlphaBasisKnotDeltaQ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.AlphaBasisKnotDeltaQ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.deltaQ_eq_h_qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.deltaQ_eq_h_qbracket","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.lean#L47-L55","doc":"**`δ_q(T_{2,k}) = h·[k]_q`** with `h = q − q⁻¹` — the pre-archimedean\nq-dimension identity (no `π`, no field). Sorry-free. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:alpha-basis-knot-delta-q","label":"prop:alpha-basis-knot-delta-q","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.qbracket","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.lean#L42-L45","doc":"Quantum integer `[k]_q = (q^k − q^{-k})·h⁻¹`, with the Hecke amplitude\n`h = q − q⁻¹` carried as a unit `h : Rˣ` (see the module note). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.deltaQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlphaBasisKnot.deltaQ","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-basis-knot-delta-q.lean#L38-L40","doc":"q-dimension decoration `δ_q(T_{2,k}) = q^k − q^{-k}`, over the substrate\nring with `q` a unit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}